# ktrans changes typed Latin letters to the letters of another language. It reads the keyboard of rio from /dev/kbdtap and writes the result back to it. In Japanese, the window of ktrans shows the words of the dictionary for the kana that are typed. The script types "nihon", and the window shows the words for the kana of nihon. The Del key in the window of ktrans stops it.
class exact
window 400x200
run ktrans -l jp </dev/kbdtap >/dev/kbdtap
pause 2
keys "nihon"
quiet
snap words
exit "\x7f"
